DATA

Files under data/ are released under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licences/by-sa/4.0/.

Why share-alike rather than CC BY. Sense glosses in the corpus derive in part
from Wiktionary, whose text is dual-licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 and GFDL; share-alike
requires material containing it to carry the same or a compatible licence. The
glosses are not confined to one file: every sense key has the form word::gloss,
so they appear in the labels, the predictions and the key list of every vector
file. Licensing the whole data directory CC BY-SA 4.0 is the simplest way to
comply everywhere at once.

Attribution. Wiktionary content: https://www.wiktionary.org/ and its
contributors, used under CC BY-SA 4.0.

WordNet. Other glosses derive from Princeton WordNet 3.0, whose licence is
permissive and compatible with CC BY-SA, and requires this notice:

  WordNet Release 3.0 Copyright 2006 by Princeton University. All rights
  reserved. THIS SOFTWARE AND DATABASE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND PRINCETON
  UNIVERSITY MAKES NO REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

Generated text. Files under data/generations/ are model output produced under
activation steering, included so the analysis can be reproduced. Some are
degenerate, and some are emotionally charged by construction. They are research
artifacts, not endorsed content.

Model weights are not redistributed; models are referenced by Hugging Face
identifier. The NRC VAD Lexicon is not redistributed and no comparison against it
is included.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

MODEL-DERIVED DATA

Model weights are not redistributed; models are referenced by Hugging Face
identifier. Some released files are nevertheless derived from the models:

  generated text      model output. The Gemma Terms of Use state that Outputs
                      are not Model Derivatives.
  activation vectors  hidden states recorded while running each model
  atlases             int8 projections of each model's unembedding matrix

We do not relicense model-derived content. The numerical content of the vectors
and atlases is distributed subject to the licence of the model it derives from;
the CC BY-SA 4.0 licence above covers what we contribute to those files (sense
keys, glosses, word lists and their arrangement). As stated on each model card
at the time of writing:

  google/gemma-3-1b-it, google/gemma-3-1b-pt,
  unsloth/gemma-2-9b-bnb-4bit            Gemma Terms of Use
  meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-8B             Meta Llama 3 Community License
  Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B                      Apache License 2.0
  mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.3              Apache License 2.0
  EleutherAI/pythia-6.9b                 Apache License 2.0
  state-spaces/mamba-2.8b-hf             Apache License 2.0
  microsoft/phi-2                        MIT License

Gemma-derived files are provided subject to the Gemma Terms of Use. The use
restrictions of its Section 3.2, including the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy
(ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy), apply to any use of those files and
are an enforceable condition of this licence for them.

Llama-derived files are provided subject to the Meta Llama 3 Community License
and its Acceptable Use Policy. Built with Meta Llama 3.

The required notices are in licences/NOTICE, and copies of every model
licence are in the licences/ folder. This section is informational and not legal advice.
